  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse multisectorielle aux inondations dans les provinces de N&#x2019;Djam&#xE9;na et Lac</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $950,000 UNICEF project is to provide WASH and child protection assistance to flood-affected Chadians in N&#x2019;Djamena and in the Lac region. To that end, UNICEF will install latrines and showers, distribute hygiene kits, install child-friendly spaces, provide psychosocial support, documentation and reunification services, and raise awareness around child protection concerns. In total, the WASH component will target 72,000 people, including 14,976 women and 22,464 girls. The child protection component will target 20,000 people, including 2,500 women and 7,000 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
